{
  "tema": 9263,
  "slug": "ya-preterito",
  "titulo": "Ya with the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "¿Ya comiste? Sí, ya comí.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Ya + preterite says something has already happened: ya comí = I already ate / I've eaten. In questions it means yet: ¿Ya comiste? = Have you eaten yet? This is the everyday Mexican way to say it.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ya** means _already_. With the preterite it says an action is done: **ya comí** = _I already ate_ / _I've eaten_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "ya",
            "+ preterite"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In questions, **ya** means _yet_: **¿Ya comiste?** = _Have you eaten yet?_"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ya** usually goes **before the verb**. It can also go at the end: **¿Comiste ya?**, but **ya** first is more common."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Where English uses _have done_ for something that just happened, Mexican Spanish usually says **ya** + preterite: **¿Ya llegaste?**, rather than **¿Has llegado?**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To answer _not yet_, use **todavía no**: **¿Ya comiste? — Todavía no.** (**Ya no** means _not anymore_.)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Ya comí==, gracias.",
              "en": "I already ate, thanks."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Ya terminaste== la tarea?",
              "en": "Have you finished your homework yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ya llegué==, estoy afuera.",
              "en": "I'm here, I'm outside."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ya vi== esa película dos veces.",
              "en": "I've already seen that movie twice."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mis papás ==ya se fueron== a dormir.",
              "en": "My parents already went to bed."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Ya pagaste== la luz?",
              "en": "Did you pay the electric bill yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ya regué== las plantas del huerto.",
              "en": "I already watered the plants in the garden."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
